Cut-card dedupe (tracker half of the duplicate fix)

A follow-up card is sent with the two-state bounded(send, slice, null), where
`null` means "we stopped waiting" — the request is still in flight and the card
is usually already in the chat. The pass read that as a failure, rolled the
row's announcement bookkeeping back, and the next pass re-derived the SAME card
and sent it again. The live duplicates (💀 REK 20:39 → 21:02 HKT, 🚀 POPEYE
18:36/18:39/18:43/18:46/18:49 HKT) all have no `followup` audit entry at all,
which is that path's signature: nothing is audited on a cut.

This half: keep the request object, write the audit entry a late success
deserves (the proof), record the attempt as a cut-card mark on the row's own
mark CSV, and refuse the re-send when the audit proves the earlier attempt
landed. Nothing proven = sent, exactly as before (never-miss).

